That should be a weapons class or a spell class.  Once I've explored
a level and I want to move around in it quickly, I tend to use the jump
spell again and again until I use up half of my manna (keeping
plenty in reserve to have combat spell ability).  Casting so many
spells is a way to enhance that school to max.  With wizards I
tend to force bolt all doors known to not lead to shops and plenty
of monsters as a way to move up that school.  For attack spells the
trade-off is whether it costs dagger advancement.

> I do something similar, but with XP 15 as the baseline.

Interesting strategy.  Should be added together with my suggested
one of viewing the maxed out levels as an endpoint.

> I also start
> my analysis from the spellcasting side and work backwards.  At that
